{
  "title": "Replace inline filter panel with a sidebar (desktop) / sheet \
(mobile)",
  "description": "The cookbook filter panel currently expands inline above the \
grid, pushing all results below the fold whenever you want to narrow by tag. \
With ~45 tag checkboxes it dominates the screen.\n\
\n\
Change:\n\
- Desktop (≥1200px after the grid-fill change lands): persistent left sidebar  \
 (~260px) with filters always visible and collapsible. Grid takes the rest.\n\
- Tablet/mobile: slide-over drawer or bottom sheet.\n\
- Render tag filters as clickable chips with an active/filled state, not   \
checkbox+label pairs. Sort by frequency or alphabetical.\n\
- Make the utility bar (search / sort / density / bulk-mode entry) sticky   \
under the app header with a blurred translucent backdrop so it stays   \
reachable while scrolling.\n\
\n\
Out of scope: the query-string contract for filters. Keep the existing \
URL-based state — that's a strength.\n\
\n\
Depends on `p2-cookbook-grid-fill-wide-displays.json5` for the space budget; \
do that first.\n\
\n\
CSS quality: the filter panel and its children have their own ~100 lines of \
one-off rules. When you rebuild as a sidebar, audit what can collapse into \
shared components (chip, form input, surface) and what genuinely needs its own \
rules. Don't leave the old `.filter-panel` CSS sitting alongside the new \
sidebar styles. See `p3-css-cleanup.json5`.",
